<head>
  <title>ErrorMDT: DTM error detection</title>
<meta content="text/html; charset=ISO-8859-1" http-equiv="Content-Type"/></head>

<body>
  <!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent al titol de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<h1><span id="wpstitol"/></h1>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent titol de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->
 <!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<span id="wpsopcions"/>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->
	
  <p>The program compares the value of each cell with the result of a local interpolation of its 4 or 8 neighbors. If this difference is high, higher than the Student's t indicated, it is marked as a suspected error location. The program generates a model with the differences in each cell and a non-structured point vector (VEC) with the locations with the possibility of being wrong. It is also possible to generate a report, in the form of a text file, which includes the list of these candidates. The verification algorithm simplifies the columns and extreme rows of the raster (column 0, row 0, last column and last row).</p>

  <p>The algorithm is based on the method proposed in the article by <b>Felicísimo Á M</b> (1994) <i>Parametric
  statistical method for error detection in digital elevation models</i> ISPRS
  Journal of Photogrammetry and Remote Sensing, 49(4):29-33, with some improvements and additional sophistication.</p>
  <hr/>
